    "body": "partial (stage 3) on issue/27-solidcore-healing · PR #849 (draft) · pinned by heal_keeps_every_fixture_at_its_closed_form, truck_offers_no_heal, native_round_trip_matches_closed_form, vertex_gap_is_closed_by_the_importer, corrupt_native_files_never_panic_or_hang, seam_refuses_degenerate_heal_and_oversized_files · merges at the next cut · `Refs #27`, so the issue stays open.\n\nReadings:\n- **Heal (solidcore against closed form; truck is Unsupported, recorded as not yet)**: 5 fixtures. They are a box, a cylinder, a box minus a through-cylinder, an L union, and a box with an r2 edge round. All are within 4.7e-8 abs, with bbox deviation 0.\n- **Native `.smb` round trip** (write, then read, heal and check): the same 5 fixtures, same numbers. STEP stays on truck-stepio.\n- **Vertex gap**: the port \"heals\" a gap of any size by growing the vertex tolerance, never by moving the vertex. Gaps of 1e-6, 1e-4 and 5e-4 import as V = 1000 exact, with the bbox carrying the gap. Gaps of 2e-3 and 1e-2 are refused by the seam's `HEAL_GAP_LIMIT` (1e-3).\n- **Corrupt corpus**: 21 files, every case under a 60 s bound, verdicts pinned. No panic, no hang. The importer refuses every corrupt file. Four whole edits (version number, final newline, zero or negative zone tolerance) import as exactly the 10-box.\n- **Port findings (pinned)**: the raw reader returns `Ok` with an EMPTY B-rep for a blank file, plain text, binary noise, a header-only file and a NaN zone tolerance. It also returns `Ok` for a box whose vertex sits 1.0 off its edges.\n- clippy -D warnings is clean. The wasm32 check passes. The quick gate is green (kernel suites only).\n\nRemaining for the gate:\n1. The wasm CI job (`workflow_dispatch`, maintainer's call on `.github`).\n2. The first production consumer switched behind the bench.\n3. Upstream reports for the pinned findings of stages 1-3.\n4. A heal bench on vendorable real-world models with curved gaps.\n5. Then truck's kernel role is retired; STEP IO stays on truck.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
