    "body": "review round 1 fixed on issue/27-solidcore-healing · PR #849 head ece27e29 (draft) · pinned by heal_refuses_nonsense_brep_tolerance (new), corrupt_native_files_never_panic_or_hang (re-pinned), seam_refuses_degenerate_heal_and_oversized_files (can no longer skip) · merges at the next cut.\n\n- The heal tolerance guard (0, -1, NaN, +inf) is now reached directly and pinned, under the 60 s bound.\n- `import_smb` returns `Imported { brep, notes }`. A zone tolerance the reader replaced or clamped is an `ImportNote` diagnostic (pinned: \"zone tolerance 0e0 replaced by 1e-4\"). Intact files are asserted against the exact 10-box, bounding box included.\n- A file with a format version newer than the port's (42) is now refused: the reader would parse a newer layout with version-42 rules. A non-finite declared zone tolerance is refused before the reader runs.\n- `vertex_gaps` counts edges with no 3D curve. The importer refuses any such edge; in-memory heal accepts them (the port's boolean results carry them), and the risk is recorded in decision 3.\n- `HEAL_GAP_LIMIT` is stated in mm and called a chosen bench limit, to revisit with real-world models (remaining item 4).\n- The provenance comment now names where the `.smb` knowledge comes from.\n- Checked in the port: it bounds every declared count against the bytes left before it allocates. Recorded as decision 5a; a new corpus file (control-point count 1e15) is refused at once.\n\nGates: release kernel suites green (import_corpus now 3 tests), clippy -D warnings clean, wasm32 check passes, quick gate green (kernel suites, 12.0 min).\n\nThe remaining list is unchanged from the stage-3 comment.\n",
