    "body": "Maintainer decision (2026-11-11): solidcore now has a STEP crate upstream (`crates/solidcore-step`, unpublished), and truck is to be replaced by solidcore for STEP as well. This supersedes \"STEP IO stays on truck\" in this issue's body and in decision 4 of `docs/decisions/27-solidcore-healing.md`. Chosen route: git pin of the solidcore workspace at one commit, bench first. Filed: #916 (stage 4: STEP import behind the seam, benched against truck) and #917 (stage 5: the app switches, truck and ruststep are removed; blocked on #916). #909 (drop the ruststep pin) closes with #917 if upstream ruststep has not released by then.",
